       while the gauge reports XDSG or PRECHARGE, so in case (i) the charge power is at most 1.2567 A x 16.884 V = 21.22 W (at the 14 V threshold, 17.59 W) (INFERRED)
     CHG_INHIBIT (HIZ) or SHORE_INHIBIT asserted while the pack cannot discharge: the converter is off, so VSYS has no source and the
       kit stops; the controllers die, the pull-downs release the line and the kit restarts: a loop (INFERRED: 9.3.8, the UVLO, the netlists)
     FW-C08 asserts SHORE_INHIBIT below 0 C: with a pack below -9 C the source start REQ-024 requires is cut by the hold itself (finding U4-F1, INFERRED)
   NOT STATED in any held document (named, not inferred): N1 VSYS's regulation and transient response with no battery under the
     kit's load steps; N2 what the converter regulates with CHRG_INHIBIT = 1 or ChargeCurrent 0 and no battery current (Q-TI-3);
     N3 whether the charger charges before any host write (Q-TI-2); N4 VSYS's effective capacitance at 16.884 V against TI's 50 uF (RECORD, MAKER);
     N5 every load converter's minimum input (A-14, R-49); N6 0-V charging before the gauge's SUV check (Q-TI-7)
   THE PACK'S STATES BY PERMISSION (B2; the gauge's own FETs, SLUUAQ3A 2.2 and 4.12) and how a charge hold is made in each (INFERRED):
     S1 charge on, discharge on: the pack and the source share the kit; a hold by the CHRG_INHIBIT bit or ChargeCurrent 0 (9.4.1) leaves the converter
        carrying the kit from the source (11): REQ-077 as written
     S2 charge on, discharge off (a warm CUV trip, or an OCD, AOLD or SCD latch): the source alone carries the kit and the pack can still take charge
        through Q2's diode, so the gauge does NOT hold the charge; a hold only by the bit or ChargeCurrent 0; whether VSYS stays regulated with charge
        inhibited while the pack cannot discharge is N2 (Q-TI-3): OPEN, the bench proves it (E11-06)
     S3 charge off, discharge on (between UTD -9 C and UTC 1 C; OTC; COV): the gauge holds the charge; a requested hold by the bit as in S1 (REQ-077)
     S4 charge off, discharge off (below -9 C, SHUTDOWN, a permanent fail, or no pack): the source alone carries the kit and the gauge already holds
        the charge. THE ONE EXCEPTION: in S4 the bit is NOT set and ChargeCurrent() is not written 0, so N2 never arises where the source alone carries
        the kit with no charge possible; the hold is the gauge's own
     THE HOLD PERSISTS ACROSS STATES: it is a flag in the firmware, set and cleared only by its own condition (the cold hold above 3 C with hysteresis,
        the operator, REQ-077's hold), never by a state change; in S1, S2 and S3 the bit follows the flag; on leaving S4 (a FET closing, a pack fitted)
        the bit is written from the flag at once, and in the firmware's reaction time only the gauge's window acts, which keeps the cells inside their
        charge window; after a charger POR ChargeCurrent() is 0 A (9.6, MAKER) and the firmware writes it only after reading the flag (INFERRED)
     in S2 and S4 the CHG_INHIBIT line (HIZ, 9.3.8) and SHORE_INHIBIT each remove the kit's only supply: neither is ever a charge hold (rule R-a)

3. U-04, THE ENTRY AT A 9.00 V PLUG, THE KIT'S OWN LOSSES AND THE SOURCE ENVELOPE (the focused check's B1 and B3)
   3a. the drawn LM5069 against a 9.00 V plug (finding U4-F2, corrected in the fix round)
     UVLOTH 2.45 / 2.5 / 2.55 V, UVLOHYS 12 / 21 / 30 uA (SNVS452G p.5); Equations 38 to 40 (p.24): the falling threshold is UVLOTH x (1 + R20/R21),
       the rising one that plus UVLOHYS x R20 (MAKER); the first round put the hysteresis on the falling edge, so its numbers and its R21 draft were wrong
     as drawn (R20 100k, R21 38.3k, 1 %): on at 9.91 / 11.13 / 12.37 V rising, off at 8.72 / 9.03 / 9.34 V falling: NOT MET at 9.00 V (INFERRED)
     the withdrawn first-round draft (R21 42.2k): on at 9.33 / 10.52 / 11.74 V rising, off at 8.14 / 8.42 / 8.71 V falling: NOT MET at 9.00 V (INFERRED)
     POREN (all functions enabled, VIN increasing) 8.4 typical, 9 V maximum; PORIT 7.6 / 8 V; POREN's hysteresis 90 mV typical; the operating range 9 to 80 V (SNVS452G p.1, p.5) (MAKER)
     U6's VIN (pin 2) is DC_P behind the ideal diode (NETLIST); before the hot swap conducts, VIN is at most 9.00 V less the LM74700's regulated drop
       (13 / 20 / 29 mV, SNOSD17G) = 8.987 V, under POREN's 9 V maximum: no divider makes a 9.00 V plug start the LM5069 (NOT MET, INFERRED)
     with the in-service current flowing DC_P falls further, to 8.43 V at the 9.00 V plug's maximum (3e), under POREN less its 90 mV typical hysteresis (INFERRED)
     the IC cannot be supplied from elsewhere: VIN is the current-sense reference (VCL is the VIN-SENSE voltage, p.5), so it sits at R19's top (MAKER, NETLIST)
   3b. what a replacement must do (INFERRED; the figures are 3d to 3e's):
     (1) operate and enable below its own supply at the in-service maximum from a 9.00 V plug, DC_P 8.43 V hot; (2) act on overcurrent between
       the in-service maximum at 9 V (5.983 A) and F1's 80 C column (7.3 A); (3) keep the pass FET inside its derated chart in every start, a start into a
       resistive fault included; (4) lock out over-voltage above CS101's 38.83 V peak and under D10's 42.4 V breakdown at -20 C (L4-E9), with a 100 V rating
     TPS1663 (SLVSET9G, held back): 4.5 to 60 V, 67 V absolute; its highest limit (RILIM 3 k) 5.58 / 6 / 6.42 A: under 5.98 A, fails (2) (MAKER)
     TPS4811-Q1 (SLUSEE5E, held back): VS 3.5 to 80 V, 100 V absolute, VS POR 2.75 / 3 / 3.2 V; EN/UVLO 1.16 / 1.18 / 1.2 V rising and 1.1 / 1.11 / 1.13 V falling,
       320 nA leakage at most; OV the same thresholds (TPS48110 only); OCP 29.2 / 30.6 / 31.5 mV at RSET 100 Ohm and RIWRN 39.7 k; ISCP bias 13.7 / 15.6 / 17.6 uA (Equation 11,
       464 Ohm); TMR 73 / 82 / 91 uA to 1.112 / 1.2 / 1.3 V, retry 22.7e6 x CTMR after 32 cycles; short-circuit response 4 / 5 us (TPS48110); charge pump 11 to 13 V;
       gate-slew inrush 0.63 x V(BST-SRC) x CLOAD / (R1 x C1) (Equation 3); input pins to 20 V absolute; TI's 100 Ohm VS filter and 1 nF CSCP (MAKER)
       it meets (1), (2) and (4); it limits no power, so (3) rests on the pass FET (3c)
